[{:db/id "q-11007/selection/e82c778ed6c65f2665dbf14b39f9573a118a56bc77e7db4679d7ce7ec32dc5fa" :answer/id #uuid "a082b5ef-4432-5a26-94b1-5ee1f5d438d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x+1}{({x}^{2}+11)}+\\frac{1}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007/selection/837c8388e68a9334b1596d4dbaeaaeb1e1a6cd93e4dd6b8a62eb3ebecbf46d72" :answer/id #uuid "6518ffc0-cff6-5554-9615-49971311022d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{4}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007/selection/712460e101185efb4082bcb6c6ed96500eda9c20d591129900d488f9e8e8f29c" :answer/id #uuid "e9e61a2e-1e40-5e75-b293-68a9203b6a77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{3}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007/selection/29b3fd533018e44257bb195b4b50a06137e0b57572cf9a7e565a74b720c73cf1" :answer/id #uuid "ebbb8a3d-56a5-5e10-94a4-7af107198885" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+5}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{7}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007/selection/100577a463cbd20ac57224229c7c9e2b4fce70e7c2c77a4816a1af7efccbefd6" :answer/id #uuid "a3f4ae5f-2a6c-567f-b63c-ad4e4959e404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+2}{({x}^{2}+11)}+\\frac{2}{(x-5)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2da4db48-0dde-5e52-941d-16512a829e1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11007/selection/837c8388e68a9334b1596d4dbaeaaeb1e1a6cd93e4dd6b8a62eb3ebecbf46d72" :answer-field/choices ["q-11007/selection/e82c778ed6c65f2665dbf14b39f9573a118a56bc77e7db4679d7ce7ec32dc5fa" "q-11007/selection/837c8388e68a9334b1596d4dbaeaaeb1e1a6cd93e4dd6b8a62eb3ebecbf46d72" "q-11007/selection/712460e101185efb4082bcb6c6ed96500eda9c20d591129900d488f9e8e8f29c" "q-11007/selection/29b3fd533018e44257bb195b4b50a06137e0b57572cf9a7e565a74b720c73cf1" "q-11007/selection/100577a463cbd20ac57224229c7c9e2b4fce70e7c2c77a4816a1af7efccbefd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11007" :question/id #uuid "ae5b3b02-16d6-5d15-8449-764655c69b3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11007" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{{x}^{2}-22x-59}{({x}^{2}+11)(x-5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-22x-59}{({x}^{2}+11)(x-5)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+11)}+\\frac{C}{(x-5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+11$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+11)(x-5)$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-22x-59=(Ax+B)(x-5)+C({x}^{2}+11).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=5$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2}-22(5)-59 & =(A(5)+B)(5-5)+C({5}^{2}+11) \\\\ 25-110-59 & =36C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{144}{36} \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}-22(0)-59 & =(A(0)+B)(0-5)+C({0}^{2}+11) \\\\ -59 & =-5B+11C \\\\ -59 & =-5B+11(-4) \\\\ 5B & =-44+59 \\\\ B & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2}-22(1)-59 & =(A(1)+B)(1-5)+C({1}^{2}+11) \\\\ 1-22-59 & =-4A-4B+12C \\\\ -80 & =-4A-4(3)+12(-4) \\\\ 4A & =-12-48+80 \\\\ A & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=5,$ $B=3,$ and $C=-4.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-22x-59}{({x}^{2}+11)(x-5)}=\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{4}{(x-5)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11007/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection/bb0e2da1ca06d6b7dd7e5a3d1f116b523b11046edbc529f39384a6e3e973b0e6" :answer/id #uuid "3afbe726-981d-5ba5-b433-35e0d24bec16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{7}{(x-11)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection/63d7cd39c01c62453cc08a4cf2ba47df32271d3272922f87cb8086666b9a8b57" :answer/id #uuid "16bcf5b2-d66a-54b2-9e2e-c0287929116f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{3}{(x-11)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection/d107e39dbdc33534760dcdfe6a4c01b5db0dd9f1fb509cf093a883a59c363de9" :answer/id #uuid "8304b930-9e9c-5a18-b212-3b6f09476633" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-11)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection/631df8e0ee486cdd59413ec5f75c0e8af50f8f9cc68411f86e8f84666e0379c1" :answer/id #uuid "e55f486a-bba8-5b12-8050-b37ad1324a60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+9}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{6}{(x-11)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection/ceff2eae0698280f1d2376eb32b2ea401e26e20520803ff333686ee2a9449f44" :answer/id #uuid "ed08a7a2-8f22-58ab-9817-a9f9a832e161" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+5}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{4}{(x-11)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "124787b1-5580-54cb-ac81-a6486c174ec7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11013/selection/63d7cd39c01c62453cc08a4cf2ba47df32271d3272922f87cb8086666b9a8b57" :answer-field/choices ["q-11013/selection/bb0e2da1ca06d6b7dd7e5a3d1f116b523b11046edbc529f39384a6e3e973b0e6" "q-11013/selection/63d7cd39c01c62453cc08a4cf2ba47df32271d3272922f87cb8086666b9a8b57" "q-11013/selection/d107e39dbdc33534760dcdfe6a4c01b5db0dd9f1fb509cf093a883a59c363de9" "q-11013/selection/631df8e0ee486cdd59413ec5f75c0e8af50f8f9cc68411f86e8f84666e0379c1" "q-11013/selection/ceff2eae0698280f1d2376eb32b2ea401e26e20520803ff333686ee2a9449f44"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11013" :question/id #uuid "c61f2d91-e7a8-56cf-8315-741d2aa72afa" :question/math-academy-id "q-11013" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{{x}^{2}-43x-20}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-11)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-43x-20}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-11)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-11)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+3)(x-11)$ and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-43x-20=(Ax+B)(x-11)+C({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=11$ eliminates $A$ and $B$ and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(11)^{2}-43(11)-20 & =(A(11)+B)(11-11)+C((11)^{2}+3) \\\\ 121-473-20 & =124C \\\\ -372 & =124C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{372}{124} \\\\ C & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}-43(0)-20 & =(A(0)+B)(0-11)+C({0}^{2}+3) \\\\ -20 & =-11B+3C \\\\ -20 & =-11B+3(-3) \\\\ 11B & =-9+20 \\\\ B & =\\frac{11}{11} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2}-43(1)-20 & =(A(1)+B)(1-11)+C({1}^{2}+3) \\\\ -62 & =-10A-10B+4C \\\\ -62 & =-10A-10(1)+4(-3) \\\\ 10A & =-10-12+62 \\\\ A & =\\frac{40}{10} \\\\ A & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=4,$ $B=1,$ and $C=-3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-43x-20}{({x}^{2}+3)(x-11)}=\\frac{4x+1}{({x}^{2}+3)}-\\frac{3}{(x-11)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11013/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11013"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11014"] :question/problem "Express $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+2x+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)$ and get\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+2x+5=(Ax+B)(x-1)+C({x}^{2}+2x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+2(1)+5 & =(A(1)+B)(1-1)+C((1)^{2}+2(1)+3) \\\\ 5+2+5 & =6C \\\\ C & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({0}^{2})+2(0)+5 & =(A(0)+B)(0-1)+C({0}^{2}+2(0)+3) \\\\ 5 & =-B+3C \\\\ 5 & =-B+3(2) \\\\ B & =6-5 \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=2$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(2)^{2}+2(2)+5 & =(A(2)+B)(2-1)+C({2}^{2}+2(2)+3) \\\\ 29 & =2A+B+11C \\\\ 29 & =2A+(1)+11(2) \\\\ 2A & =29-23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=1,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)}=\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "597bbd6d-c369-53a2-b7c2-caa98f65cfd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "b4f3fd82-0d58-5910-bd74-06cf4d52f82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1f0c5739-0f9e-547a-b9f3-f4fd615b41ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e27cc934-f5b8-57b0-8a1b-0f041a4e4e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "7f65bf20-562c-570a-a767-7bb3923b9704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "522ba403-f89e-56c6-a15a-20e298d3f6dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49724/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-49724/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-49724/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-49724/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-49724/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-49724/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49724" :question/id #uuid "7d761b54-6320-55f1-b7ed-30330f572d09" :question/math-academy-id "q-49724" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}+9}{({x}^{2}+3)x}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{C}{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, find the value of $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+3)x$ and get\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}+9=(Ax+B)x+C({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)^{2}+9 & =(A(0)+B)(0)+C({0}^{2}+3) \\\\ 9 & =3C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ and using our result for $C$ gives us an equation for $A$ in terms of $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)^{2}+9 & =(A(1)+B)(1)+(3)({1}^{2}+3) \\\\ 11 & =A+B+12 \\\\ A & =-B-1.\\,\\,(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1$ and using our result for $C$ gives us another equation for $A$ in terms of $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}+9 & =(A(-1)+B)(-1)+(3)((-1)^{2}+3) \\\\ 11 & =A-B+12 \\\\ A & =B-1.\\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the equations $(1)$ and $(2)$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-B-1 & =B-1 \\\\ -2B & =0 \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we use our result for $B$ in equation $(2).$ We get\n\n$$\nA=(0)-1=-1.\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1,$ $B=0,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\nA+B+C=-1+0+3=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5a864707-d5cb-523e-8971-2242d17049cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b2ea9441-7ce8-56c5-a27c-f9a13ba031ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "0a4fcc99-0942-551e-8c1b-315971ef5729" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "53b23b03-0494-583b-b395-95cf280a3791" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "9402b7d7-312c-51bc-aced-3b869b69a242" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6de8ce-7452-5b79-9a56-e20a20c1d18e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102560/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-102560/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-102560/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-102560/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-102560/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-102560/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102560" :question/id #uuid "8ca29016-576b-5531-978a-0e93b6677e56" :question/math-academy-id "q-102560" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5x+12}{(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)}=\\frac{x+B}{2{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{2}{x-3},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-5x+12 & =(x+B)(x-3)+2(2{x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)^{2}-5(0)+12 & =(0+B)(0-3)+2(2(0)^{2}+3) \\\\ 12 & =-3B+6 \\\\ 6 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102560/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102560"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
